# Deployment parameters for this rig — the single source of truth.
#
# Read by: server.py (via python-dotenv), mcp-run.sh (which launches the MCP server),
# the Makefile (via -include), and set_env.sh. Change a value here and every one of
# them follows. A real environment variable always wins over anything set here, so
# `GOOGLE_CLOUD_ZONE=europe-west4-a make status` still works for a one-off.
#
# Zone note: flex-start v5litepod-1 is only accepted in us-west4-a. europe-west4-a and
# europe-west4-b both reject it at the API. See the gotcha in CLAUDE.md before changing.

GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT=aisprint-491218
GOOGLE_CLOUD_REGION=us-west4
GOOGLE_CLOUD_ZONE=us-west4-a

# The QAT-at-q4_0 build, shipped as bf16 safetensors — the "-unquantized" suffix is the
# whole point: the tensors on disk are 16-bit, so vLLM loads them through the ordinary
# unquantized path. A real Q4_0 GGUF will NOT load on this stack; see README.md.
MODEL_NAME=google/gemma-4-E2B-it-qat-q4_0-unquantized
ACCELERATOR_TYPE=v5litepod-1
TENSOR_PARALLEL_SIZE=1

# Name of what this rig provisions: the Queued Resource id for the MCP tools (its node is
# <RESOURCE_ID>-node) and, as SERVICE_NAME, the tpu-vm for the Makefile's separate path.
# Left unset, both derive from the rig directory name — tpu-vllm-v5e1-2b-q4_0. Set them only to
# reach a resource created under an older name; a rename otherwise orphans it.
# Deliberately blank: this rig is new, so there is no older resource to reach back to, and
# the template's examples pointed at the tpu-vllm-v5e1-2b rig's own resources.
#RESOURCE_ID=
#SERVICE_NAME=

# Name this rig's MCP server advertises, and the key the client must register it under —
# that key prefixes every tool, as mcp__<name>__find_tpu. Left unset it derives from the rig
# directory (tpu-vllm-v5e1-2b-q4_0), which is what keeps the six sibling rigs distinguishable;
# they previously all registered as "tpu-devops". Set it only to match a client that has
# already registered this server under a different key. `make mcp-config` writes a .mcp.json
# using the same value.
#MCP_SERVER_NAME=tpu-vllm-v5e1-2b-q4_0

# Default provisioning model for the Queued Resource tools: flex-start, spot, or on-demand.
# Every creation tool takes a provisioning_model argument that overrides this per call.
#   flex-start - queues for scarce capacity, self-terminates after 4h. v5litepod-1 is only
#                accepted in us-west4-a; see the zone note above.
#   spot       - cheapest, drawn from the separate preemptible quota (TPU_SPOT_QUOTA_ID),
#                reclaimable with ~30s notice, and NOT bounded by max-run-duration.
#   on-demand  - full price, no preemption, also unbounded. Destroy it yourself.
PROVISIONING_MODEL=flex-start
